From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gpl: regression tests for timing paths that global placement
 leaves on a detour
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Not upstreamed. Test-only: new files under src/gpl/test and new targets
in its BUILD.

- path_shape.{h,cpp}, a testonly cc_library: synthetic designs built in
  odb (no LEF, DEF or liberty) whose good path shape is known, a path
  from a fixed launch register to a fixed capture register through k
  clusters started in each of their k! orders, through broadcast drivers
  with up to 37 side loads, or against side nets that pull its clusters
  the wrong way; the metrics (detour, cluster order, HPWL against the
  known placement, a period proxy); and a hook that puts timing weights
  on the path's nets before the Nesterov loop, without STA. Where the
  right order of two clusters depends on the weights, it is computed,
  not read off a rule: the weighted HPWL of both orders over every legal
  place of the two clusters, and a case whose orders are within 5 % of
  each other is refused as a tie.
- path_shape_test: the invariants, 56 tests that pass today and must
  keep passing after any change that makes gpl more robust (90 s on one
  core, fastbuild).
- path_shape_targets_test: the targets, 44 tests, tagged "manual". Every
  test in it fails today by design, each on its own threshold. Both
  print one line per check:
    METRIC <test> <name>=<value> <op> <threshold> pass|FAIL
  Run the targets by name:
    bazelisk test @openroad//src/gpl/test:path_shape_targets_test
  A gpl change that makes a target pass moves it to path_shape_test.

Nothing //:openroad or //src/sta:opensta is built from is touched, so the
openroad binary every ORFS stage runs keeps its cache key.

Retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that carries these tests (or the
fix they are written for, with its own tests); if a bump changes the gpl
API the weight hook uses (PlacerBaseCommon, NesterovBaseCommon,
NesterovPlace) the patch is rebased or dropped, not worked around.
Held with 0221, whose pin_pull_test builds on these; they go upstream
together.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
